 "notes": [
  "Frequencies are hertz, both ends inclusive. Every range was read from the e-CFR text of 47 CFR Part 97 current to 2026-09-23 (last amended 2026-02-13).",
  "Only the HF bands Aether uses are encoded, for a station in ITU Region 2 (the continental United States, Alaska and Hawaii). A station elsewhere is refused rather than judged against the wrong table.",
  "The 80 m and 75 m bands of §97.301 are one band here, 3.5-4.0 MHz: a signal across 3.600 MHz is outside the data segment, not outside the band."
 ],
 "bandwidth": {
  "rule": "§97.3(a)(8)",
  "reading": "wider",
  "why": "§97.3(a)(8) defines bandwidth as the width of a band outside of which the mean power is at least 26 dB below the mean power within it. Read as a ratio of powers it is the band holding all but 1/398 of the power; read as a spectral level it is where the density falls 26 dB below the mean density within the band. The two differ for Aether's narrow emissions (the tone floor: 434-445 Hz against 551-557 Hz), so the wider of the two decides."
 },
